>
>Spoilers hereinafter:

>
>Specialized Artifacts:
>	These do double damage against one class of monster, normal against
>	all others.  Thus, all that matters is the weapon type.

What should be noted here is that the damage is doubled AFTER
calculating bonuses for the enchantment and blessings on the weapon.
For instance, if I am attacking a non-fire-resistant undead with my
blessed +8 fire brand (I have strength 18/99), the minimum damage is:

2 * (1 + 8 + 1) + 5 = 25

and the max (for small) is

2 * (8 + 8 + 4) + 5 = 45!

However, as I descend into hell, I notice that many of the denizens
tend to be fire resistant.  Fortunately, my god seems to like black
puddings, and before they were auto-genocided, he gave me a frost
brand.  This hero runs hot and cold!!

It might be nice to have a message mentioning the effect of those
weapons that some monsters are or are not resistant to:

The fiery blade burns the hill orc!  (with Fire Brand)
The icy blade chills the Minotaur!  (for Frost Brand)
...and so on...

for non resistant monsters, and normal messages for resistant
monsters as Stormbringer currently works:

You hit the fire ant!      (with Fire Brand)
You hit the white dragon.  (with Frost Brand)

...in other news...

BTW, as someone mentioned, it would be really fun to put a fortune in
there that says

"It will be a cold day in Hell when someone steals the Amulet."

Or better yet...

You take the Amulet of Yendor -more-
The snowball hits!

I like the idea.... You need fire resistance to get into Hell, but you
need cold resistance to get out.  Actually, if you read Dante's Divine
Comedy (the Inferno cantos), you'll see that the very deepest levels
of Hell are icy cold, with the tortured souls frozen solid in blocks
of ice, not even able to move.

